<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/2nd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cimbrian War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">113–101 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cimbrian War was fought from 113 to 101 BCE between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a> and the migrating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cimbri">Cimbri</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutones">Teutones</a>. The tribes inflicted several defeats on Roman armies, worst at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orange-vaucluse">Arausio</a> in 105 BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaius-marius">Gaius Marius</a>, repeatedly elected consul, reformed the army and destroyed the Teutones at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aix-en-provence">Aquae Sextiae</a> in 102 BCE and the Cimbri at Vercellae in 101 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cimbrian-war.jpg" alt="Cimbrian War" width="320" height="272" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pethrus · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cimbrians_and_Teutons_invasions.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
